thority / stakeholder / decision owner.\n- **Coda** remains Strategic Governance: organizational coherence, authority boundaries, framework integrity, canon/supersession, cross-seat reconciliation, and Don decision framing. Coda does **not** absorb technical methodology, architecture, operations, verification, or implementation. fileciteturn8file0L1-L9\n- **Kimi/Corrado** owns methodology.\n- **Chiave** owns architecture where architecture is materially required.\n- **Principal Consultant** translates/specifies; it does not redesign upstream work.\n- **Calibro** owns implementation design inside accepted upstream contracts.\n- **Talon** owns operational routing/control.\n- **Keel/build resources** execute.\n- **Luce** independently determines supportable truth/evidence.\n- **Coda governs across the chain** rather than acting as another production hop.\n\nThere is one artifact-level inconsistency worth remembering but **not solving today**: `01_GCE_FRAMEWORK_CURRENT` still contains the older combined Kimi “Methodology / Design & Build” language and marks the separation of methodology from concrete design as a proposed refinement. The later operational material we already loaded resolves that working model much further—Principal Consultant → Calibro → Talon, etc. So when an older framework doc disagrees with the later settled operating state, I will flag the provenance rather than accidentally reverting us.\n\nAnd most importantly, **where we actually left off was not organizational cleanup.**\n\nThe September 11 closed record had already moved well beyond “what is our team?” The team had done the isolation-first pass, bootstrapped back into real seats, attacked the concept, and deliberately narrowed the experiment. The packet says the working conclusion was: the concept was coherent enough to test, engineering was cheap relative to behavioral uncertainty, the experiment could be designed to lose, discontinuities appeared to be the strongest potential value area, overbuilding would be a mistake, and **BUILD had to be earned**. fileciteturn4file0L292-L313\n\nThe next planned move was therefore:\n\n**Freeze the smallest honest manual experiment → Session 0 → one real manual discontinuity test → independent verification → STOP / REVISE / MORE MANUAL / BUILD MINIMAL.** No code first. fileciteturn4file0L317-L386\n\nSo for Don, I would mark the new-week restart like this:\n\n**Last meaningful Framework work:** Thursday, **September 11, 2026**.  \n**Gap:** Sept. 12–13 — Framework essentially idle.  \n**Restart:** Monday, **September 14, 2026 — Luxor**.  \n**Current mission:** recover the live conceptual state gently, then resume the **manual-first shared-state / B2B coordination experiment** from the pre-sprint checkpoint.  \n**Not the mission:** reorganize every Framework document, clean every folder, re-litigate seats, or build software.\n\nThat’s the context I’ll use from here. We can let **this conversation become the living Framework thread for the new week**, while Drive remains the artifact/provenance layer.\n\n**STATUS:** PROCEED  \n**CONFIDENCE:** 98%  \n**REASON:** The current framework spine and September 11 stopping point are consistent enough to resume without reopening the broader organization.  \n**NEXT GATE:** Re-enter the Sept. 11 sprint state and decide what Don wants to execute first on 9/14.  \n**DON INPUT NEEDED:** No framework clarification required.", "text_chars": 4404, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "bb2beaf3-626c-4e65-8ecf-13b015a26bdd", "role": "tool", "role_name": "api_tool.call_tool", "created_at": 1789411982.7992992, "updated_at": 1789412013.64652, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "code", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citatio